      "writtenOn": "2021-10-05T21:26:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no. it subtracts this value from stack pointer. it can fail if there is not enough stack, but this would same with static array. I want to remove all artificial limits to RSA 3K/4K without increasing stack consumption when it is not needed. With alloca() I can support RSA 3K/4K if needed by enterprise teams (still need to allow this for TPM), but for currently used RSA 2K it won\u0027t add to stack use.",
